.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn xft_next_pow2 0 ,
.Fn xft_last_pow2 0 ,
.Fn xft_next_pow2
of a value above 2^63,
and
.Fn xft_roll_mask
with
.Fa chunk_size
\-
.Fa n
outside 0 to 63 are undefined behavior, as they shift by 64 or more.
.Pp
On x86_64,
.Fn xft_popcount_*
use the
.Ql popcnt
instruction unconditionally.
.Pp
The portable
.Fn xft_memclz_u128 ,
used on x86_64 without
.Dv __BMI__ ,
ignores the upper 64 bits of
.Fa x
and returns 64 plus the leading zero count of the lower half.
